From 739e61f1783125c018222307eeb769f64ff8c78c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Catalin Niculescu <cn.cata@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:16:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] LUT sweep: CUDA GPU load, load x fan sweep, fan_lut.json
 builder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- research/gpu_stress.cu: an FMA-bound kernel at a duty cycle (about 113 W
  on the RTX 4080 Laptop GPU at 100 %); built with -U_GNU_SOURCE because
  glibc 2.43 and CUDA 13.0 declare rsqrtf differently.
- research/lut_sweep.py: from full load down to idle (100/70/40/20/0 %),
  the pad at 100/60/30/0 % at each, GPU then CPU; settles after each load
  change, writes the CSV row by row, always stops the load and puts the
  fan back before releasing, stops at 92 °C on the GPU.
- research/build_lut.py: per load, the slowest fan within 1.5 °C of the
  coolest without extra throttling, keyed by the temperature it runs at;
  the higher of the CPU's and GPU's speeds leads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
